Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: it's often fragmented and vulnerable,

987
00:51:03,440 --> 00:51:08,080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: especially when it comes to changes in political leadership and congressional priorities.

988
00:51:08,080 --> 00:51:12,080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Hence, the intention of...

989
00:51:12,260 --> 00:51:33,720
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of CAPE, which will serve as a cross-committee and cross-party platform where shared education reform agenda can be discussed will also translate to evidence and recommendations from EDCOM 2 and other education stakeholders, including oversight initiatives, budget priorities, and sustained policy action.

990
00:51:33,720 --> 00:51:41,980
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Ultimately, the case for supporting CAPE rests on a simple principle, and that is education reform requires more than good policies.

991
00:51:41,980 --> 00:51:53,680
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: It requires a durable coalition capable of carrying those policies from evidence to legislation, from legislation to funding, from funding to implementation, and accountability.

